{"slug":"setup-task-system","title":"The Task System","blocks":[{"id":"b1","type":"ingress","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Barkpark as your AI's task board: the agent claims work over HTTP, you steer the same queue in the browser Studio, and every change broadcasts to both sides in real time."}]},{"id":"b2","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Tasks are plain "},{"type":"text","value":"type:task","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" documents — no second store, no sync. A root task is a "},{"type":"text","value":"goal","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"; children nest under it; dependencies form a graph; claims are atomic and fenced so many workers can't trample each other."}]},{"id":"b3","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"What you get"},{"id":"b4","type":"table","head":[[{"type":"text","value":"Surface"}],[{"type":"text","value":"What"}]],"rows":[[[{"type":"text","value":"Studio Tasks pane","marks":["strong"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"text","value":"Tasks ✅","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" desk group at "},{"type":"text","value":"/studio","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (plugin desk item), with lifecycle tabs (open · in_progress · blocked · closed · all). The editor is a full dossier in four groups — "},{"type":"text","value":"brief","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" (description, design notes, an expandable "},{"type":"text","value":"design_doc","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" paper reference, checkable acceptance criteria with met/evidence), "},{"type":"text","value":"work","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" (priority, assignee, estimate, due date, labels), "},{"type":"text","value":"close","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" (outcome, reason), "},{"type":"text","value":"system","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — plus soft validations (e.g. closing "},{"type":"text","value":"done","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" without an outcome warns). "},{"type":"text","value":"dependencies","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"text","value":"claim","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" render read-only (\"managed via API\")."}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"bp","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" verbs","marks":["strong"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"bp task ls / ready / get / next / claim / close","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — manifest-driven from "},{"type":"text","value":"GET /v1/capabilities","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", provenance "},{"type":"text","value":"plugin:tasks","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Terminal TUI","marks":["strong"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"Task lists carry quick actions: "},{"type":"text","value":"c","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" claims the highlighted task, "},{"type":"text","value":"x","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" closes it (same fenced endpoints; worker id from "},{"type":"text","value":"BARKPARK_WORKER_ID","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", default "},{"type":"text","value":"tui-<hostname>","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"). Plus the standard desk keys — "},{"type":"text","value":"/","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" search, "},{"type":"text","value":"n","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" new, "},{"type":"text","value":"y","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" duplicate, "},{"type":"text","value":"D","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"×2 delete."}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"HTTP API","marks":["strong"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"Eleven bearer-token endpoints under "},{"type":"text","value":"/v1/tasks/*","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (read tier, not admin): list, ready-queue, "},{"type":"text","value":"prime","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" (one-call agent rehydration), queue claim, targeted claim, close, fetch-with-children, edges, labels, paper links."}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Events","marks":["strong"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"Every task op emits a "},{"type":"text","value":"mutation_events","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" row — "},{"type":"text","value":"task.claimed / task.closed / task.mutated / task.relabeled / task.referenced / task.lease_expired","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — streamed over SSE at "},{"type":"text","value":"/v1/data/listen/:dataset","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]]]},{"id":"b5","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Lifecycle states: "},{"type":"text","value":"open · in_progress · blocked · done · cancelled","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":"b6","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Set up from zero"},{"id":"b7","type":"code","value":"curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FRIKKern/barkpark/main/scripts/install-cli.sh | sh\nbp            # no config + TTY → the setup wizard, then the TUI"},{"id":"b8","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The wizard's "},{"type":"text","value":"clean profile pre-checks the bulldocs and tasks plugins","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" (the server unions "},{"type":"text","value":"media","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" in on its own). Accept, and the task schema, routes, and cron workers are live on first boot. Already running a dev server on "},{"type":"text","value":":4000","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"? It blocks the local target's DB reset — stop it first, or pick "},{"type":"text","value":"connect","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" instead."}]},{"id":"b9","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Existing installs","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — enable via env and restart:"}]},{"id":"b10","type":"code","value":"BARKPARK_PLUGINS=bulldocs,tasks    # CSV whitelist · unset = all plugins · empty = kill switch"},{"id":"b11","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"Server (deploy.sh / bp setup --target deploy):","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" pass "},{"type":"text","value":"BARKPARK_PLUGINS=bulldocs,tasks","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" in the deploy env — it persists into "},{"type":"text","value":"/opt/barkpark/.env","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", sourced by "},{"type":"text","value":"api/start.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (the systemd unit's ExecStart)."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Docker:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"docker-compose.yml","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" passes the variable through as a bare "},{"type":"text","value":"- BARKPARK_PLUGINS","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" entry — export it in the invoking shell before "},{"type":"text","value":"docker compose up","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Local mix:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"BARKPARK_PLUGINS=bulldocs,tasks mix phx.server","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]]},{"id":"b12","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"text","value":"task","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" schema auto-registers on every boot (idempotent on "},{"type":"text","value":"(name, dataset)","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"); two Oban cron jobs come with it — a lease sweeper every minute and compaction every six hours."}]},{"id":"b13","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Point an AI agent at it"},{"id":"b14","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Token.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Any bearer token works for the task endpoints (read tier — claim/close are workflow ops, not document mutations). Creating tasks goes through the mutate endpoint, which needs an admin token. Dev default: "},{"type":"text","value":"barkpark-dev-token","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":"b15","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Discover.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" One call teaches the whole surface:"}]},{"id":"b16","type":"code","value":"bp capabilities -o json          # or: curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" $API/v1/capabilities"},{"id":"b17","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Create tasks.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Tasks are documents — create them through the standard mutation envelope. Required content: "},{"type":"text","value":"kind: \"task\"","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and a valid "},{"type":"text","value":"lifecycle_status","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Optional: "},{"type":"text","value":"priority","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (0–4, 0 = highest), "},{"type":"text","value":"assignee","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"parent_id","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"labels","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"papers","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", plus the dossier fields ("},{"type":"text","value":"description","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"design","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"design_doc","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" paper slug, "},{"type":"text","value":"acceptance_criteria","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" list, "},{"type":"text","value":"estimate","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"due_at","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"outcome","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", …) — the schema ("},{"type":"text","value":"GET /v1/schemas/:dataset","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", name "},{"type":"text","value":"task","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") is the authoritative field list."}]},{"id":"b18","type":"code","value":"curl -X POST $API/v1/data/mutate/production \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"mutations\":[{\"create\":{\"_type\":\"task\",\"_id\":\"t1\",\"title\":\"Ship the docs\",\n       \"content\":{\"kind\":\"task\",\"lifecycle_status\":\"open\",\"priority\":1}}}]}'"},{"id":"b19","type":"callout","tone":"info","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Draft prefix note:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"create","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" always lands as a draft (stored id "},{"type":"text","value":"drafts.t1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"). The task endpoints resolve the bare id "},{"type":"text","value":"t1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" automatically — you can use either "},{"type":"text","value":"t1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"text","value":"drafts.t1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". If both a published "},{"type":"text","value":"t1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and a draft "},{"type":"text","value":"drafts.t1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" exist, "},{"type":"text","value":"t1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" matches the published row (exact match wins). Task lifecycle is independent of draft/publish; publishing a task is optional."}]},{"id":"b20","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"4. The claim → work → close loop.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Pick a stable "},{"type":"text","value":"worker_id","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" per agent."}]},{"id":"b21","type":"code","value":"# Queue claim: atomically take the NEXT ready task (priority ASC, then oldest)\nbp task next agent-1                # prints the claimed doc_id + epoch; no_ready on empty queue\ncurl -X POST $API/v1/tasks/claim \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"worker_id\":\"agent-1\"}'\n# → {\"ok\":true,\"doc\":{...,\"claim\":{\"worker\":\"agent-1\",\"ts_iso\":\"…\",\"epoch\":1}}}\n# → {\"ok\":false,\"reason\":\"no_ready\"} when the queue is empty\n\n# Targeted claim: name the row\nbp task claim t1 agent-1            # args: <doc_id> <worker_id>\n\n# ... do the work ...\n\n# Close: CAS on the fencing epoch you were handed at claim time\nbp task close t1 agent-1 1          # args: <doc_id> <worker_id> <observed_epoch> [lifecycle_status]"},{"id":"b22","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The contract, precisely:"}]},{"id":"b23","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"Claim","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" flips "},{"type":"text","value":"lifecycle_status","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"text","value":"in_progress","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and stamps "},{"type":"text","value":"content.claim = {worker, ts_iso, epoch}","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". The epoch bumps on "},{"type":"text","value":"every","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" claim (losing a race → 409 "},{"type":"text","value":"stale_claim","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Close","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" requires "},{"type":"text","value":"worker_id","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" + "},{"type":"text","value":"observed_epoch","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (string ints accepted). Epoch mismatch → 409 "},{"type":"text","value":"fenced_off","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — the only protection against a stale-but-alive worker writing after its lease was swept. Optional body: "},{"type":"text","value":"lifecycle_status","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"text","value":"done","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"text","value":"cancelled","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"text","value":"blocked","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", default "},{"type":"text","value":"done","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") and "},{"type":"text","value":"observed_rev","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Leases expire.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" A sweeper runs every minute; claims idle past "},{"type":"text","value":"task_lease_ttl_seconds","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (default "},{"type":"text","value":"300","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":") are released and emit "},{"type":"text","value":"task.lease_expired","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Finish or re-claim."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Ready","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" means: "},{"type":"text","value":"lifecycle_status","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" ∈ {"},{"type":"text","value":"open","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"blocked","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"} "},{"type":"text","value":"and","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" every outbound "},{"type":"text","value":"blocks","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" edge points at a "},{"type":"text","value":"done","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" task. Closing a task "},{"type":"text","value":"done","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" auto-flips dependents from "},{"type":"text","value":"blocked","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" → "},{"type":"text","value":"open","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" when their full blocker set is done."}]]},{"id":"b24","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"5. Dependencies, labels, papers.","marks":["strong"]}]},{"id":"b25","type":"code","value":"# t2 waits on t1 (from = dependent, to = blocker; kind defaults to \"blocks\")\ncurl -X POST $API/v1/tasks/edges -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"from_id\":\"drafts.t2\",\"to_id\":\"drafts.t1\"}'\n\ncurl $API/v1/tasks/drafts.t2/edges -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\"   # ?kind=all for every edge kind\n\ncurl -X POST $API/v1/tasks/drafts.t1/labels -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"add\":[\"sprint-3\"],\"remove\":[]}'\n\n# Link a paper (a Bulldocs doc) to a task — design notes travel with the work\ncurl -X POST $API/v1/tasks/drafts.t1/papers -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"add\":[\"design-notes\"]}'"},{"id":"b26","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"6. Filtered reads.","marks":["strong"]}]},{"id":"b27","type":"code","value":"bp task ready --limit 5                          # the unblocked queue\nbp task ls --limit 20                            # everything, goals included\ncurl \"$API/v1/tasks?lifecycle_status=open&label=sprint-3\" -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\"\ncurl \"$API/v1/tasks?parent=drafts.g1\" -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\"   # a goal's rail, oldest first"},{"id":"b28","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Filters: "},{"type":"text","value":"kind","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"lifecycle_status","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"phase_id","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"parent","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"label","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"type","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"limit","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (index default 1000; "},{"type":"text","value":"ready","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and the bp verbs default 50)."}]},{"id":"b29","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"7. Watch the stream.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Subscribe to "},{"type":"text","value":"/v1/data/listen/:dataset","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (SSE) and react to "},{"type":"text","value":"task.claimed","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"task.closed","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"task.lease_expired","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", etc. — no polling."}]},{"id":"b30","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Working with your AI in Studio"},{"id":"b31","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Open "},{"type":"text","value":"/studio","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" → the "},{"type":"text","value":"Tasks ✅","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" group. The division of labour:"}]},{"id":"b32","type":"table","head":[[{"type":"text","value":"You (Studio form)"}],[{"type":"text","value":"The agent (API)"}]],"rows":[[[{"type":"text","value":"Flip "},{"type":"text","value":"lifecycle_status","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (5-state dropdown), set "},{"type":"text","value":"priority","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"assignee","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", edit titles/descriptions"}],[{"type":"text","value":"claim","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"text","value":"close","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" with fencing, add edges, relabel, link papers"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Triage: open new tasks, cancel dead ones"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Drain the ready queue in priority order"}]]]},{"id":"b33","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The terminal TUI edits the flat fields (title, description, lifecycle, priority, …) and carries the claim/close quick actions ("},{"type":"text","value":"c","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"text","value":"x","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" on a task list or in a task's editor — same fenced endpoints the agent uses); composite dossier fields like "},{"type":"text","value":"acceptance_criteria","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" are Studio- and API-editable only (the documented v1 TUI constraint). "},{"type":"text","value":"dependencies","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"text","value":"claim","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" show as read-only pretty-printed JSON in the editor — round-tripping structured values through a text input would corrupt them, so the form simply never submits those fields and the API stays the single writer. Everything updates live via PubSub: when the agent claims a task, your pane reflects it without a refresh."}]},{"id":"b34","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Goals and phases"},{"id":"b35","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Everything is a task. The pattern:"}]},{"id":"b36","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"Goal","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" = a root task (no "},{"type":"text","value":"parent_id","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Phase / subtask","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" = a task whose "},{"type":"text","value":"content.parent_id","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" is the parent's doc id."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Rail","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" = a task's chronological children: "},{"type":"text","value":"GET /v1/tasks?parent=<id>","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (oldest first), and "},{"type":"text","value":"GET /v1/tasks/:id","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" returns one level of "},{"type":"text","value":"children","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" summaries inline ("},{"type":"text","value":"doc_id","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"title","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"lifecycle_status","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") plus "},{"type":"text","value":"child_count","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Scope a worker to one phase: "},{"type":"text","value":"POST /v1/tasks/claim","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"text","value":"{\"worker_id\":\"agent-1\",\"phase_id\":\"<phase-doc-id>\"}","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"text","value":"GET /v1/tasks/ready?phase_id=…","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]]},{"id":"b37","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Goal → phases → leaf tasks, with "},{"type":"text","value":"blocks","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" edges sequencing the phases, gives you a multi-phase project board in a standard Barkpark install."}]},{"id":"b38","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Workspaces, projects, datasets — experiment without mess"},{"id":"b39","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Spin up an isolated sandbox in one command — experiments stay fully isolated from your real work (deleting a whole workspace is on the deferred ledger; today spikes are abandoned in place, never leaked). Any write-tier token may create a workspace — it arrives ready to use:"}]},{"id":"b40","type":"code","value":"bp workspace create Spike\n# → workspace + you as owner-member + a Default project + a production dataset\n#   (slug derived from the name; explicit: --slug spike)\n\nbp -w spike workspace project-create agents-v2    # member-gated; -w names the workspace\nbp workspace ls                                   # what your token can reach\n# Raw HTTP equivalents: POST /api/workspaces {\"name\":…} and\n# POST /api/workspaces/:slug/projects {\"name\":…} — see docs/cheatsheets/http-api.md"},{"id":"b41","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Scoped Studio lives at "},{"type":"text","value":"/w/:workspace_slug/p/:project_slug/studio","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"; scoped data routes mirror under the same prefix. The flat "},{"type":"text","value":"/v1/tasks/*","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" surface operates on the server's default (unscoped) scope — under scoped pipelines, task reads and claims are strictly filtered by workspace + project. Membership is the boundary: non-members get 404, never an existence leak."}]},{"id":"b42","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Troubleshooting"},{"id":"b43","type":"table","head":[[{"type":"text","value":"Symptom"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Cause → fix"}]],"rows":[[[{"type":"text","value":"No "},{"type":"text","value":"Tasks","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" pane in Studio"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Plugin not whitelisted ("},{"type":"text","value":"BARKPARK_PLUGINS","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" set without "},{"type":"text","value":"tasks","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") "},{"type":"text","value":"or","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" the "},{"type":"text","value":"task","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" schema isn't registered in this dataset. Fix env, restart; the schema auto-registers on boot."}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"404","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" on "},{"type":"text","value":"/v1/tasks/*","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"Plugin disabled — routes only mount when the tasks plugin is registered."}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"404 task not found","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" on an id you just created"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Rare — the endpoints resolve bare "},{"type":"text","value":"t1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"text","value":"drafts.t1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" automatically. Check that the task plugin is enabled and the token has access."}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"400 worker_id is required","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"Claim/close need "},{"type":"text","value":"worker_id","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — positional via bp ("},{"type":"text","value":"bp task claim <id> <worker>","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"), JSON body via curl."}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"409 fenced_off","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"Your "},{"type":"text","value":"observed_epoch","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" is stale — the lease was swept and re-claimed. Re-claim, then close with the new epoch."}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"409 stale_claim","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"Lost a concurrent claim race. Call "},{"type":"text","value":"/v1/tasks/claim","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" again."}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"409 not_ready","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"Targeted claim on a task that is "},{"type":"text","value":"in_progress","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":"done","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":"cancelled","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"409 blocked_by_unsatisfied_deps","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"Targeted claim while a "},{"type":"text","value":"blocks","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" edge points at a non-"},{"type":"text","value":"done","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" task."}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"{\"ok\":false,\"reason\":\"no_ready\"}","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"Not an error — the queue is empty (HTTP 200)."}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Task invisible in Studio but in API"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Tenancy: the doc carries a different workspace/project scope than the Studio you're looking at."}]]]},{"id":"b44","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Cheatsheet: "},{"type":"text","value":"../cheatsheets/tasks.md","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" · CLI canon: "},{"type":"text","value":"../cli/HANDBOOK.md","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" · HTTP contract: "},{"type":"text","value":"../api-v1.md","marks":["code"]}]}],"related":["decisions-deferred","cheatsheets-http-api","cheatsheets-tasks","cli-handbook","api-v1"]}
